Notes about Debian's slapd package
----------------------------------

OpenLDAP 2.1 includes the new BDB database backend which is also the
recommended backend to use. In comparision to the formerly recommended
LDBM backend (which still exists for compatibility reasons), it is
supposed to be both faster and safer to use, i.e. hot backups are now
possible with the BDB database backend.

To switch to the BDB backend, you should export your current database
in LDIF format with the slapcat command (be sure to stop slapd before
doing so), move the old database files away, change /etc/ldap/slapd.conf,
and then reimport your database from the LDIF file via slapadd.

 -- Roland Bauerschmidt <rb@debian.org>  Fri, 14 Feb 2003 18:36:16 +0100

